# Tracer: malformed input can be corrected in the same live Session.
#
# Before (the malformed declaration stopped the REPL):
# have a R
# have fn incomplete_function(x R) R = x +
# Former outcome: session_terminated: true; later input could not be submitted.
#
# Now: the CLI regression submits that rejected declaration, verifies a $in R,
# then submits this corrected declaration under the same name in one process.
have a R
have fn incomplete_function(x R) R = x + 1
incomplete_function(2) = 3
#
# Boundary: malformed input remains rejected and publishes no declaration.
# Parsing stops the current submission; the next REPL submission can continue.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -strict -lang en -f examples/stmt_nodes/definition/session_input_recovery.lit
# Recovery gate: cargo test --release --test cli_feedback session_recovers_incomplete_functions_tokenizer_errors_and_proof_misses
